   "id": "r7",
   "page": 1,
   "source": "layout-regroup",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "text": "‘Redlands Trailblazer’ arose from a selection and controlled\npollination program between 1978 and 1990. Selection\nwas primarily for virus resistance and agronomic\ncharacteristics. Resistance was transferred from Cucurbita\necuadorensis. Following final selection, two generations of\nopen pollination have established ‘Redlands Trailblazer’ as\na variety.",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
