  {
   "id": "r9",
   "page": 1,
   "source": "layout-regroup",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "text": "‘Redlands Trailblazer’ is an open pollinated vine type\npumpkin. It is resistant to zucchini yellow mosaic virus,\nwatermelon mosaic virus, and papaya ringspot virus type\nW. lt is moderately branched with moderate vigour, and\nhas medium green, reniform ieaves with no marbling. The\nleaves of ‘Redlands Trailblazer’ are shorter, and have\nthinner petioles, than those of ‘Queensland Blue’ and\n‘Jarrahdale’.",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
      309.84,
      164.4,
      520.56,
      173.52
     ],
     "text": "‘Redlands Trailblazer’ is an open pollinated vine type"
